      {
        "id": 14108,
        "name": "Radman The Lucario",
        "username": "Radman_The_Lucario",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/radman_the_lucario/{size}/2462_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-14T18:31:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Can you really speedrun the video game version of a tabletop card game? I say, of course you can! :P</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>With the idea of a 'campaign' of sorts from the recent survey, it's sort of pushed this idea a bit further for me. First thing needed is some ground rules for single games:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Categories will be split by villain and number of heroes on your team (Ex. Fighting Baron Blade with 4 heroes, or Omnitron with 5)</li></ul><ul><li>Timing starts on clicking 'Start Game' in the actual fight itself, and stops on the fade to the victory screen.</li></ul><p>What is allowed:</p><ul>\n<li>Any combination of heroes in any turn order.</li>\n<li>Any environment.</li>\n<li>Seeing your heroes cards before starting the game itself (and restarting to get an acceptable first draw)</li>\n</ul><p>What is NOT allowed:</p><ul>\n<li>Rewinding (gotta keep going forward)</li>\n<li>Pausing the timer mid run (You can pause your game, but the timer must keep running)</li>\n</ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Just some preliminary thoughts on rules for runs. Anyone have any additions or questions, let me know. :)</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:46:06.237Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
