        "raw": "<p>Can you really speedrun the video game version of a tabletop card game? I say, of course you can! :P</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>With the idea of a &#39;campaign&#39; of sorts from the recent survey, it&#39;s sort of pushed this idea a bit further for me. First thing needed is some ground rules for single games:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Categories will be split by villain and number of heroes on your team (Ex. Fighting Baron Blade with 4 heroes, or Omnitron with 5)</li></ul><ul><li>Timing starts on clicking &#39;Start Game&#39; in the actual fight itself, and stops on the fade to the victory screen.</li></ul><p>What is allowed:</p><ul><li>Any combination of heroes in any turn order.</li><li>Any environment.</li><li>Seeing your heroes cards before starting the game itself (and restarting to get an acceptable first draw)</li></ul><p>What is NOT allowed:</p><ul><li>Rewinding (gotta keep going forward)</li><li>Pausing the timer mid run (You can pause your game, but the timer must keep running)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Just some preliminary thoughts on rules for runs. Anyone have any additions or questions, let me know. :)</p>",
